# {{.SiteName}}

This is a complete, white-label documentation product built around one explicit route tree. The generated project demonstrates durable Markdown, nested navigation, GoFastr composition, OpenAPI, local search, offline delivery, testing, deployment, and AI-assisted authoring in the same shell.

## Start with the route tree

Open the [getting started guide](/docs/getting-started), then move through the Concepts, Build, Operate, and Collaborate sections in the sidebar. Every page in this handbook is a real route, searchable from the native `Meta/Control + K` command palette, and available to the offline shell.

## The product model

`docs.Router` is the source of truth. It knows what the site is, how it is ordered, how it is searched, and which rendering strategy each surface uses. A page can be Markdown, a typed screen, or a plugin contribution without creating a second navigation system.

## What to explore

- **Concepts** explains the router, authoring model, and nested layouts.
- **Build** covers screens, OpenAPI, and extensions.
- **Operate** covers search, offline delivery, testing, and deployment.
- **Collaborate** documents the agent references and authoring skill.
- **Examples** turns the model into practical product-surface checklists.
